**Plan, not yet applied.**

`buildRows()` in [report.js](src/report.js:11) gives full rows, `owner` and `slow` included. `toTable()` in [format.js:7](src/format.js:7) only prints `id, suite, status, ms` by design.

```js
// cli.js
const flagIdx = argv.indexOf('--json');
const json = flagIdx !== -1;
const rows = buildRows();
process.stdout.write((json ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2) : toTable(rows)) + '\n');
```

Open question: should `--json` include `owner` and `slow`, which the table hides, or match the table's four columns exactly. "Same data" in your ask suggests full rows.

Say which you want and I'll apply it.
